course: dictionary
lesson: 2845
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as numbered meanings, and the sentence around the word shows which one the writer means. «A doctor cannot feel your pain» is about a person who helps sick people, not about a person with a university degree.
explain: Doctor can also mean a person with the highest university degree, shown as Dr. As a verb, doctor means to change something in a sneaky way, as in «doctored photos». Ask yourself: does the health meaning make sense here, or does the sentence need a different meaning?
explain: In health, a doctor checks your body, gives advice and may give medicines. «Pain that starts round the belly button and moves to the bottom right side, with fever, can be appendicitis and needs a doctor.» The clues are pain, fever and needs, so the health meaning fits.
fact: Doctor (noun) means a person trained to look after people who are ill or hurt and to help them get better.
fact: Vets are doctors for animals.
fact: Useful phrases: go to the doctor, see a doctor, family doctor, GP (British), doctor's appointment.
fact: Doctor (verb) means to change something in a sneaky way, as in «doctored photos».
fact: Only take medicine that a doctor or trusted adult gives you.
exercise: «A doctor cannot feel your pain, so say clearly where it hurts.» What does doctor mean here? | A person who changes photos sneakily | A teacher who gives homework | *A person trained to help people who are ill or hurt | A person who sells medicine in a shop
exercise: Mia says the photo was doctored. What does doctored mean? | *Changed in a sneaky way | Taken with a very good camera | Sent to a doctor for a check | Printed on thick paper
exercise: «In a hospital or doctor's waiting room you speak quietly and stay seated.» Find and copy the one word that means sitting down. | quietly | waiting | *seated | hospital
test: Why should you only take medicine that a doctor or trusted adult gives you? | Medicine tastes nicer from a stranger | Medicine from a stranger is always safe | Doctors never give medicine | *Medicine must be right for you, and a doctor or trusted adult knows what is safe
test: Sara says a fish hook should be pulled out at home. Why should an adult or doctor remove it instead? | Fish need the hook back | The hook is shiny and might get lost | Doctors like collecting hooks | *The barb, the little backward hook on its point, tears skin
exam: In «doctors treated the swelling», what does doctors mean? | *People trained to look after people who are ill or hurt | People who change things in a sneaky way | Helpers who only look after pets, with no link to people | A person with the highest university degree
